  "title": "Expired Orders Cause Stale Price Discovery in getTOB() Leading to Griefing Attacks and Market Data Corruption",
  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n\n### Root Cause Analysis\n\nThe vulnerability stems from incomplete cleanup of expired orders in the Red-Black Tree price level management system, directly affecting the critical getTOB() function that external systems rely on for market data:\n\n- **Incomplete Price Level Removal:** In Book.sol::_updateLimitRemoveOrder(), price levels are only removed when numOrders == 1, meaning only when removing the very last order at that price level.\n- **Stale Price Level Persistence:** When expired orders are removed but other orders remain at the same price level, the price level stays in the tree even if all remaining orders are also expired.\n- **Unfiltered External Price Discovery:** The getTOB() function returns stale prices from expired orders to external systems without any expiration filtering.\n\n### Code Evidence & Impact Chain\n\n### ICLOB Interface \n\n```solidity\ninterface ICLOB {\n    // This function exposes stale price data to external systems\n    function getTOB() external view returns (uint256, uint256); // maxBid, minAsk\n}\n\n```\n\n###  Book.sol:\n\n```solidity\nfunction _updateLimitRemoveOrder(Book storage self, Order storage order) private {\n    // ...\n    if (limit.numOrders == 1) {\n        // Price level only removed if it's the LAST order\n        if (order.side == Side.BUY) {\n            delete self.bidLimits[price];\n            self.bidTree.remove(price); // Only removes when numOrders == 1\n        } else {\n            delete self.askLimits[price];\n            self.askTree.remove(price); // Only removes when numOrders == 1\n        }\n        return;\n    }\n    //  BUG: Price level persists even when all remaining orders expire\n}\n\n```\n\n### Clob.sol\n\n```solidity\nfunction getBestAskPrice(Book storage self) internal view returns (uint256) {\n    return self.askTree.minimum(); // -- No expiration filtering\n}\n\nfunction getBestBidPrice(Book storage self) internal view returns (uint256) {\n    return self.bidTree.maximum(); // -- No expiration filtering\n}\n\n// getTOB() calls these functions and exposes stale data externally\nfunction getTOB() external view returns (uint256 maxBid, uint256 minAsk) {\n    maxBid = getBestBidPrice(book);   // -- Returns stale expired prices\n    minAsk = getBestAskPrice(book);   // -- Returns stale expired prices\n}\n\n```\n\n\n### Attack Scenario:\nMalicious actors can:\n\nPlace multiple orders at strategic price levels\nAllow orders to expire while keeping price levels \"alive\"\nForce the system to maintain many stale price levels\nDegrade system performance and increase gas costs for legitimate users\n\n### Impact:\n- **External View Functions:**\n    - `getTOB()` - Returns potentially stale best bid/ask prices\n    - `getOrdersPaginated()` - May start iteration from expired order heads\n- **Internal Price Discovery:**\n    - `getBestAskPrice()` / `getBestBidPrice()` - No expiration filtering\n    - Matching engine functions encounter extra cleanup iterations\n- **Tree Management:**\n    - `_updateLimitRemoveOrder()` - Incomplete price level cleanup\n    - Red-Black Tree maintains stale price levels\n\nDuring order matching, the system encounters additional overhead:\n\n```solidity\nwhile (bestAskPrice <= incomingOrder.price && incomingOrder.amount > 0) {\n    Order storage bestAskOrder = ds.orders[limit.headOrder];\n\n    if (bestAskOrder.isExpired()) {\n        _removeExpiredAsk(ds, bestAskOrder); // Extra cleanup work\n        bestAskPrice = ds.getBestAskPrice(); // Re-query price\n        continue; // Wasted iteration\n    }\n    // ... actual matching\n}\n\n```\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n\n```solidity\nfunction getBestAskPrice(Book storage self) internal view returns (uint256) {\n    uint256 price = self.askTree.minimum();\n    while (price != type(uint256).max) {\n        // Check if head order at this price is active\n        if (!self.orders[self.askLimits[price].headOrder].isExpired()) {\n            return price;\n        }\n        price = self.askTree.getNextBiggest(price);\n    }\n    return type(uint256).max; // No active asks\n}\n\n```\n\nApply similar logic to getBestBidPrice() and consider implementing proactive cleanup mechanisms to prevent stale price level accumulation.",
